  "reference": "Qwen2.5-0.5B for languages, SmolLM2-135M for English (the protocol of the earlier corpora).",
  "screening": "Each candidate, in its family's seeded order, is prepared with small quotas (train 2^23*1.05, ref_stats 2^21) and screened: c = h_ref(512 tokens) / ngram23, with h_ref from 1,000 targets of the reference model at 512 tokens of context and ngram23 the best n-gram cross-entropy trained on 2^23 bytes (the paper's definitions). A candidate is eligible when c < 0.70. A candidate whose screening fails (stream, preparation or the reference's byte check) is ineligible.",
  "selection": "The first 20 eligible candidates of each family in seeded order are the study corpora; later eligible candidates are spares in the same order.",
  "replacement": "A study corpus that fails full preparation, its statistics or its reference pass is replaced by the next eligible spare of its family in seeded order (screening continues down the order if the spares run out); if the family's order is exhausted the slot is dropped.",
  "training_order": "Interleaved: language 1, English 1, language 2, English 2, ... (positions in each family's final list).",
  "cost_cut": "If the projected all-in spend exceeds the $3.50 cap, corpora are dropped from the end of the interleaved order in language/English pairs, never below 30 corpora in total; if 30 cannot be afforded, the run stops and is reported.",
